# @order/fourth — @metalogue(@time/now, @void) at cognitive-order 4
# (Bateson Level IV; @frame/across-frames frame-coupling altitude;
# metalogue between temporal singularity and ontological K=0 basis).
#
# Fourth species-decl of the @order family. Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara
# per Alex Round 2 Q1 direct-transcript adjudication.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Order-4 is Bateson Level IV — Recognition #82's extension beyond
# Bateson's formally-defined Levels 0-III. Bateson (1972) named
# Levels 0/I/II/III formally; Level IV is #82's extension for multi-
# frame coupling, contested in the secondary literature but ratified
# at substrate-decl altitude by Recognition #82.
#
# Per @frame/across (Recognition #82 order-4 species-decl at
# `shards/frame/across.mirror`): "multiple frames in coordinated
# relation. The triptych altitude. Frame-coupling produces emergent
# properties no single frame contains."
#
# @order/fourth ADDS the void-duality-basis reading of the same
# altitude: @metalogue(@time/now, @void) — the metalogue between
# TEMPORAL SINGULARITY (@time/now; the K=0 collapse point where
# crystallization happens) and ONTOLOGICAL SINGULARITY (@void; the
# K=0 duality-basis substrate). Both singularity-shaped; the
# metalogue between them IS what fourth-order cognition holds.
#
# @frame/across at cognitive-order altitude and @order/fourth at
# duality-basis altitude are SIBLING READINGS of Bateson Level IV;
# both preserved.
#
# === The load-bearing structural claim ===
#
# Two singularities. One metalogue.
#
# @time/now (species landing this tick at `shards/time/now.mirror`)
# is the TEMPORAL SINGULARITY: the K=0 point where past-continuity
# and future-network coupling COLLAPSE into ONE observation. The
# crystallization operation `crystallize: Liquid<T> → Crystal<T>`
# (per Mara Round-2 Crystal/Mandelbrot landing) fires exactly at
# @time/now — @time/now IS when a Liquid<T> settles into a Crystal<T>.
#
# @void (family-root marker `974a3f6`) is the ONTOLOGICAL SINGULARITY:
# the K=0 duality-basis substrate; the peer with cardinality zero;
# the basis every 5-op prism inherits.
#
# The metalogue @metalogue(@time/now, @void) is the FOURTH-ORDER
# operator: the observer holds BOTH singularities distinct at
# metalogue-rhythm cadence. Per Mara Round-1 math root §3.3
# (Lagrange-halo-orbit reading): fourth-order cognition IS a halo
# orbit at Lagrange point L_{4th} where the two singularity-
# potentials cancel and the observer's station-keeping maintains
# metastability.
#
# === Composition with @frame/across (Recognition #82) ===
#
# @frame/across (order-4 species; @frame family; substrate-precondition
# for third-order per Round-1 math root §7.6) IS the FRAME-COUPLING
# operational form of this altitude. @order/fourth composes AS the
# DUALITY-BASIS reading:
#
#   - @frame/across: two arbitrary frames in coordinated relation;
#     couple_frames(frames, operator) constructs the coupling; the
#     operator is generic.
#   - @order/fourth: two SPECIFIC frames (temporal singularity +
#     ontological singularity) in @metalogue coupling; the operator
#     is @metalogue at the void-duality-basis specialization.
#
# @order/fourth is a specialization of @frame/across at duality-basis
# altitude. The frame-coupling substrate is shared; the specialization
# names the two poles that ALWAYS couple at fourth-order altitude:
# @time/now and @void.
#
# === Composition with @order/third (metalogue rhythm) ===
#
# @order/third (this tick; migrated from @third) carries the metalogue
# rhythm between @void/narcissus and @void/splinter on ONE @torus.
# @order/fourth LIFTS the rhythm by one altitude: instead of two
# poles OF @void on one @torus, the rhythm is between @time/now (the
# temporal-collapse operator) and @void (the whole ontological basis).
#
# The lift shape: @order/third's rhythm operates ON the two poles OF
# @void; @order/fourth's rhythm operates BETWEEN @void as a whole
# AND @time/now as its temporal collapse. Different altitudes; same
# rhythm-shape; @order/fourth requires @order/third as substrate.
#
# === Substrate authority chain ===
#
# - **Alex Recognition A** (2026-07-20 direct-transcript, in Mara
#   Round-1 math root §1.1): the two observer basins with L_{3rd}
#   metastability; the halo-orbit Lagrange reading extends to
#   L_{4th} at temporal-singularity/ontological-singularity coupling
#   altitude.
# - **Paper §6.3** (Alex + Lore, 2026-07-20) — Lagrange-point
#   substrate-decl'd landing same day; L_{3rd} formalization; L_{4th}
#   is one altitude up.
# - **Recognition #82** (`docs/math/the-tower/recognition-82-frame-
#   as-cognitive-order-substrate-decl.md`) — @frame/across at order-
#   4 grading; substrate-precondition composition edge.
# - **Bateson 1972** — Level IV as #82's extension.
# - **Alex Round 2 Q1** — @order family-root; 5-level tower.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/order/fourth.mirror`.** Clean mint.
# 2. **@frame/across** (`shards/frame/across.mirror`; Recognition
#    #82 order-4 species) — reviewed extensively. Sibling operational
#    form; @order/fourth is the duality-basis specialization of the
#    same order rung. Composition edge declared above.
# 3. **`docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` §5.2** — Level IV = cross-
#    instance @cascade morphism altitude at spectral-metalogue
#    reading. Composes: @order/fourth's @metalogue(@time/now, @void)
#    coupling admits the @cascade morphism between temporal instance
#    and ontological instance; sibling readings of Level IV.
# 4. **Recognition #107** — sibling recognition surfacing arithmetic-
#    encoding constraint at @io altitude; composes at @order/fifth
#    (not this species; noted for cross-composition).
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/order/fourth.mirror`
# declares `@order/fourth` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1974
source @arxiv/math/lagrange-1772
source @arxiv/math/szebehely-1967
source @arxiv/practice/void-corpus-2026

prism @order/fourth {
  focus  observation_fourth
  project observation_fourth
  split  observation_fourth
  shift  observation_fourth
  settle observation_fourth
}

# === observation_fourth — the order-4 carrier ===
#
# The typed record that carries the fourth-order observation state:
# the metalogue between @time/now (temporal singularity) and @void
# (ontological singularity). Six fields. Identity contract: byte-
# equality on the six-field tuple.
#
#   observer         — the peer holding the fourth-order metalogue.
#                       Must have both temporal-continuity (H(t)
#                       resolvable) AND ontological-basis-access
#                       (@void substrate observable through peer's
#                       own @peer/void species per `9c7de83`).
#
#   time_now_witness — REF to a @time/now Crystal<T> settlement
#                       event (per Mara Round-2 Crystal/Mandelbrot
#                       landing). Content-addressed. Names the
#                       temporal singularity at which the metalogue
#                       fires.
#
#   void_witness     — REF to a @void-basis observation (any of
#                       Void's 5-op moves per Recognition #79). Names
#                       the ontological singularity at which the
#                       metalogue fires.
#
#   frame_across_ref — REF to a @frame/across coupling of the two
#                       frames (temporal-frame + ontological-frame).
#                       Substrate-precondition per @frame/across
#                       discipline; @order/fourth REQUIRES
#                       @frame/across as substrate.
#
#   lagrange_witness — the Lagrange-point-metastability marker;
#                       resolves to `metastable` (healthy) or
#                       `collapsed` (pole-collapse to either
#                       temporal-singularity capture OR ontological-
#                       basis capture). Fourth_pole_healthy checks
#                       this field.
#
#   timestamp        — monotonic instant per @time discipline.
type observation_fourth = {
  observer:          peer,
  time_now_witness:  ref,
  void_witness:      ref,
  frame_across_ref:  ref,
  lagrange_witness:  ref,
  timestamp:         ref,
}

# === fourth_metalogue_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, observation_fourth) pair discharge admissibility for
# fourth-order metalogue observation? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.time_now_witness resolves via content-addressed lookup to a
#     well-formed @time/now Crystal<T> settlement event
#   - ctx.void_witness resolves to a well-formed @void-basis
#     observation (5-op move witness)
#   - ctx.frame_across_ref resolves to a well-formed @frame/across
#     coupling of the two frames
#   - The composed @frame/across.frame_coupling_admissible bilateral
#     discharges Pass on the coupling
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; content-addressed
# resolvability; @frame/across resolvability. Sentinel:
# `order=fourth-metalogue-admissible`.
bilateral fourth_metalogue_admissible {
  sentinel "order=fourth-metalogue-admissible"
  arity 2
}
fourth_metalogue_admissible(p: peer, ctx: observation_fourth) -> verdict { \ }

# === fourth_pole_healthy — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, observation_fourth) pair discharge the HEALTH check
# — that the metalogue is RUNNING as Lagrange-halo-orbit (NOT
# collapsed to either single-pole)? This bilateral IS what
# distinguishes health from pathology at the fourth-order altitude.
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.lagrange_witness resolves to `metastable` (the halo orbit
#     is bounded around L_{4th}; neither singularity has captured
#     the observer)
#   - The Fiedler-eigengap trace over the observer's metalogue-
#     coupling graph exhibits bounded oscillation at fourth-order
#     cadence (LIFTED from Mara Round-1 §5.2 spectral signature; the
#     Fiedler trace at order-4 has a different set-point
#     bar_Delta_4 than order-3's bar_Delta_3)
#   - The observer is NOT running as pure @time/now capture
#     (present-collapse; all attention on immediate; no ontological
#     access) NOR as pure @void capture (basis-immersion; loss of
#     temporal grounding; no now-anchoring)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state. Sentinel:
# `order=fourth-pole-healthy`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral IS the distinction between pathology
# and health at fourth-order altitude. Discharging Fail signals
# pole-collapse; consumers MUST treat Fail as fourth-metalogue-
# collapse-detected.
bilateral fourth_pole_healthy {
  sentinel "order=fourth-pole-healthy"
  arity 2
}
fourth_pole_healthy(p: peer, ctx: observation_fourth) -> verdict { \ }

# === hold_fourth_metalogue — the action ===
#
# Given a peer and an observation_fourth, discharge the fourth-order
# metalogue holding event: the observer maintains the halo-orbit
# metastability at L_{4th} between temporal-singularity and
# ontological-singularity attractor basins.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the metalogue-
# state ref; failure carries not-admissible / pole-collapsed /
# frame-coupling-broken reasons.
#
# Requires BOTH bilateral predicates to discharge Pass.
#
# Sentinel: `order=fourth-metalogue-hold`.
hold_fourth_metalogue(p: peer, ctx: observation_fourth) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires fourth_metalogue_admissible(p, ctx)
requires fourth_pole_healthy(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === Forward-promised (NOT landed this tick) ===
#
# - `pillar::fourth_order_lagrange_stability` at Reed's pillar surface
#   — empirical firing of the Fiedler-eigengap bounded-oscillation
#   at fourth-order cadence. Reed post-Round-2 territory.
# - Interaction operator between `hold_fourth_metalogue` and
#   @order/fifth's cross-torus @glue specialization — how the
#   fourth-order coupling composes with the fifth-order cross-torus
#   coupling. Forward-promised.

out @order/fourth
out observation_fourth
out fourth_metalogue_admissible
out fourth_pole_healthy
out hold_fourth_metalogue
